  "findings": [
    {
      "action": "A control test name is a token only when it is absent from the visible files, and a correction line is significant only when its characters are absent from the visible text as a substring. 32 false positives to 0, with the planted-token test still passing, so the detector still detects.",
      "id": "W4-F1",
      "observed": "The scanner reported 32 leaks across 30 assembled provider prompts, all false. Two causes, both the same shape as W2-F2: a published test name that the hidden suite reuses (test_exact_multiple) was treated as secret, and a correction line that is a prefix of the baseline line it replaces was reported as a golden-source leak because the scan is a substring search.",
      "status": "fixed",
      "subject": "control-token scanner"
    },
    {
      "action": "Both adapters now send the caller's schema when the request carries one, and return that payload unread for the caller to validate. The default advisory path is byte-for-byte unchanged.",
      "id": "W4-F2",
      "observed": "Both hardcoded the C2 advisory JSON schema and ignored ModelProviderRequest.response_schema, then re-validated the reply through AdvisoryResult. A caller asking for its own structured shape was answered in a shape it had not asked for, and read the mismatch as a malformed answer rather than as the wrong schema.",
      "status": "fixed",
      "subject": "Claude Code and Codex CLI adapters"
    },
    {
      "action": "Split into boundary_failures, schema_invalid and diff_invalid, derived from what the run recorded and re-readable from an older evidence file.",
      "id": "W4-F3",
      "observed": "One `malformed` bucket held provider-availability failures and unusable diffs together. Section S21C3-043 requires model, schema, quota, rate and boundary outcomes reported separately, and a single bucket let a 9-in-10 adapter failure read as a 9-in-10 wrong-answer rate.",
      "status": "fixed",
      "subject": "provider statistics"
    },
    {
      "action": "Every apply failure is caught and recorded as malformed/diff_invalid.",
      "id": "W4-F4",
      "observed": "apply_file_patch raises DiffPolicyError on a context mismatch rather than returning None, so the campaign would have crashed on the commonest provider mistake instead of recording it as an outcome.",
      "status": "fixed",
      "subject": "provider answer classification"
    }
  ],
  "finished_at": "2026-07-30T07:45:29.013629+00:00",
