  "intent": "S21C3-032 provider diversity campaign, one attempt per task, no retries",
  "items": [
    "S21C3-040",
    "S21C3-041",
    "S21C3-042",
    "S21C3-032",
    "S21C3-043"
  ],
  "observations": {
    "every_executed_patch_was_correct": "15/15",
    "note": "Not a claim that the hidden suite is weak: it is the same suite that failed 90 of 150 offline runs in W3, including 60 patches written to satisfy the published tests exactly. It means these thirty single-edit tasks are inside the capability of both CLI providers, so this corpus does not discriminate between them and must not be used to rank them. A corpus that separates frontier providers is a D1 problem."
  },
  "providers": [
    "claude-code",
    "codex-cli",
    "openrouter"
  ],
  "reliability": {
    "fallback_policy": "No fallback provider is configured for the campaign and no result from one provider is ever attributed to another. Every recorded outcome names the provider that produced it in RealityCandidateManifest.provider_id.",
    "openrouter_failure_split": {
      "boundary": 9,
      "detail": "nine of ten calls failed inside the adapter with ProviderInvalidResponseError before any answer existed: the free route returned a response the normalizer refused. That is provider availability, not repair ability, and it is reported as its own class so it cannot be read as a wrong answer.",
      "diff_invalid": 1,
      "diff_invalid_detail": "one reply parsed and produced a diff whose hunk counts disagreed"
    },
    "openrouter_on_the_critical_path": false,
    "retry_policy": "maximum_attempts is 1 and no retry loop exists in the campaign. A campaign that retried until it liked the answer would report the number of attempts it was willing to make rather than the provider's accuracy.",
    "when_a_paid_or_pinned_provider_would_be_justified": "Not yet, and not on these numbers. A paid or pinned OpenRouter route would be justified when a C3 measurement actually depends on OpenRouter \u2014 for example a cross-provider weak-label comparison in D1 where a 9-in-10 boundary failure rate makes the comparison unmeasurable rather than merely poor. It would not be justified to improve the accuracy figure: the two CLI providers already answer this corpus, and buying a better OpenRouter score would be paying for a number, not for evidence. If it is taken up, the decision needs its own ADR, since it changes maximum_spend_usd, which every layer currently defaults to zero.",
    "why": "The 200-outcome corpus was completed in W3 from 150 offline coding outcomes and 64 re-executed governed benchmark cases, none of which touches a network. OpenRouter contributed 0 executed outcomes here and the corpus threshold was already met, so its failure delayed nothing."
  },
